A||||8||Gold-86SE||Door Hinge||||5||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||11-01-2001||09:12 AM||||<BR>I have removed a portion of the top hinge on the driver door of my 85GT.<P>There is a part that bolts to the door, a part that bolts to the A piller, and the hinge pin and bushings hold the two together.<P>The hinge pin and bushings were bad, so I removed them. I replaced the bushings with new, and I am trying to use a decent used hinge pin from another door.<P>Now when I put the everything together (while the door sits on the floor) the hinge is very loose and has a lot of play. The part of the hindge that bolts to the A piller moves up and down with the hinge pin.  To me this appears to be incorrect.  Can somebody help?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||11-01-2001||09:18 AM||||The hinge/bushing sets are available at your local parts place.  Look for the HELP brand blister packs #238407.  They are CHEAP!!!!<P>I believe the Ogre has an article in his cave which may help you along. (link at top of page).<BR>Gary||||reg||13
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||11-01-2001||02:16 PM||||<BR>I read ogre's stuff, but it did not address my concerns about the upper hinge.<P>Does anyone know.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||gomobile||11-01-2001||03:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gold-86SE:<BR><B><BR>I read ogre's stuff, but it did not address my concerns about the upper hinge.<P>Does anyone know.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I recently replaced all my hinges and did NOT run into any problems. My question to you when u say u replaced it with another. Is this part an old part or is it a GM part. Very important cause HINGES do not move up and down once they are in place. Unless the hole (bushing) is bad?<P>||||reg||6
Z||000004||Gold-86SE||11-01-2001||03:48 PM||||Question: when u say u replaced it with another. Is this part an old part or is it a GM part.<P>Answer: The bushings are brand new from a local Chevy dealership, same part from Pontiac, but Pontiac's computers were down for maintenance. The pin, is a used pin from another Fiero door.<P>Further: The new bushings fit solidily in the holes on the hinge bolted to the door, yet when I take the hinge that bolts to the A piller and connect them with the pin, it does move up and down (quite freely I might add). BTW, the door is sitting on the floor, it is not bolted to the Fiero.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodrv6||11-01-2001||04:03 PM||||You made me curious, so I just went and looked at mine.  I assume you're talking about the hinge being able to slide freely up and down along the pin, and not sideways.  In other words, the pin is a good fit in all the holes.  If that's the case, I wouldn't worry about the up and down movement.  The lower hinge seems to be designed to have little up and down play while the upper one has at least 1/4 inch or so.  Probably to account for production variations in the distance between the hinges.  Unless you invert the car (hard on the roof panel <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), you shouldn't notice any play once the door is installed.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gold-86SE||11-01-2001||04:34 PM||||<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I assume you're talking about the hinge being able to slide freely up and down along the pin, and not sideways. In other words, the pin is a good fit in all the holes. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes this is the situation.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||11-01-2001||07:16 PM||||The upper hinge is supposed to have virticle free play. the bottom one two. You'll take up some of it with the washer in my cave article. (Washer the bottom hinge only.)<P>Don't worry about the play up top. let the bottom hinge and the washer take the axial load. It's allot stronger than the top. It can handle it.<P>With what the door weighs, it's not going anywhere....<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gold-86SE||11-02-2001||09:03 AM||||<BR>I was able, with the help of my wife, to put the driver door back on the Fiero last night.<P>Every thing seems fine. I guess, as it was stated before, that it is natural to have some up/down play in the upper hinge.<BR>||||reg||1
